  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Justice for All 2026-2029</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Program by Pathfinders for Peaceful, Just and Inclusive Societies, which hosts the secretariat of the Justice Action Coalition (JAC). 

Following the review in 2025 of the JAC and further discussions in the Board meeting (Warsaw, June 2025) as well as the High Level Meeting (Madrid, November 2025) the secretariat has developed a leaner approach more adapted to the new global realities. 
The programme aligns with the new Dutch policy note as it connects the promotion of people centered justice in light of the security and stability interest. When people can solve daily disputes and grievances in a timely and people friendly way, this contributes to the early de-escalation of tensions and potential conflict, improves predictability of justice solutions and thus contributes to a stable environment and trust in institutions (social contract). 

The programme will continue to invest in the Justice Action Coalition by providing thought leadership, strengthening the global movement on justice, and convening key actors at global, regional and national levels on people-centered justice. 

The Netherlands has been spearheading the PCJ movement - in particular via the Justice Action Coalition. Under the current programme the Netherlands takes a step back, but by continuing our financial support NL can through PFI contribute to the consolidation of the global movement of people centered justice and its regional alliances. This investment should lead to further ownership and independence of the movement. Proven models by the JAC will be further implemented and linkages with national governments will be strengthened. The Netherlands foresees a less prominent role in the JAC in the future and thus anticipates this will be the last phase with (substantial) financial support for the JAC.

PFI is uniquely placed in the NYU to be a spill between governments, multilateral organisations, (private) donors and (CSO) expert partners.  The continuation of this partnership is based on the track record of PFI in the JAC and also because the JAC has been co-created by the Netherlands. The JAC has been successful in the promotion of people centered justice models providing space for innovations to tackle the justice gap. Further engaging national governments will contribute to dedicated policies and budget people centered Justice.</narrative>
  </description>
